{"id": "tea:tirumantiram:1823", "source": "src:tirumantiram", "location": {"ref": "1823", "chapter": "tantra 7"}, "paraphrase": "For the bountiful Lord the heart is the sanctum, the fleshly body the temple, the mouth the tower-gate; to those who have understood, the soul is the Śiva-liṅga, and the five deceiving senses are the lamps.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "body-layers"], "practices": ["prc:antaryaga"], "notes": "Opening 'uḷḷam peruṅkōyil ūṉuṭampu ālayam'; verse number moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirumantiram:2104", "source": "src:tirumantiram", "location": {"ref": "2104", "chapter": "tantra 9 (placement low confidence)"}, "paraphrase": "Mankind is one family and God is one; think only good; there is no death (Yama) to fear; there is no other refuge — abide steadily in the mind and be saved.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics", "ultimate"], "disputes": ["dsp:women-caste-liberation"], "notes": "Opening line 'oṉṟē kulamum oruvaṉē tēvaṉum' ('one family, one God') is certain; verse number and the rest of the paraphrase moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirumantiram:2397", "source": "src:tirumantiram", "location": {"ref": "2397"}, "paraphrase": "The Veda and the Āgama are both true, both the Lord's scripture; one is general, the other special.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "sound-language"], "disputes": ["dsp:agama-veda-authority", "dsp:status-of-veda"], "notes": "Content moderate confidence; verse number low confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirumantiram:270", "source": "src:tirumantiram", "location": {"ref": "270", "chapter": "tantra 1", "section": "aṉpuṭaimai (on love)"}, "paraphrase": "The ignorant say love and Śiva are two; none knows that love itself is Śiva; when they know that love is Śiva, they abide as love, as Śiva.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "original": {"text": "அன்பும் சிவமும் இரண்டென்பர் அறிவிலார் அன்பே சிவமாவது ஆரும் அறிகிலார் அன்பே சிவமாவது ஆரும் அறிந்தபின் அன்பே சிவமாய் அமர்ந்திருந் தாரே", "script": "Tamil", "edition": "from memory; to be checked"}, "terms": ["trm:anpu", "trm:civam"], "teachers": ["tch:tirumular"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirumantiram:63", "source": "src:tirumantiram", "location": {"ref": "63", "chapter": "pāyiram"}, "paraphrase": "The Āgamas I received are nine: Kāraṇam, Kāmikam, Vīram, Cintam, Vātuḷam, Yāmaḷam, Kālōttaram, Cuppiram and Makuṭam.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "notes": "The list of nine Āgamas is recalled with moderate confidence; the verse number is low confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirumantiram:724", "source": "src:tirumantiram", "location": {"ref": "724", "chapter": "tantra 3"}, "paraphrase": "If the body perishes the life-breath perishes and firm true knowledge cannot be reached; knowing the means to nourish the body, I nourished the body and so nourished the soul.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["body-layers", "practice"], "practices": ["prc:tirumantiram-astanga-yoga"], "notes": "Opening 'uṭampār aḻiyil uyirār aḻivar'; verse number moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirumantiram:85", "source": "src:tirumantiram", "location": {"ref": "85", "chapter": "pāyiram (preface)"}, "paraphrase": "May the world obtain the bliss that I have obtained.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "notes": "'yāṉ peṟṟa iṉpam peṟuka ivvaiyakam'; verse number moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirumantiram:tantra.1", "source": "src:tirumantiram", "location": {"ref": "tantra.1"}, "paraphrase": "The first tantra teaches the guru's greatness, the impermanence of body, wealth and youth, and conduct: non-killing, not eating flesh, not coveting another's wife, not drinking, giving, learning and love.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["ethics"], "practices": ["prc:kollamai", "prc:pulal-maruttal"], "terms": ["trm:kollamai", "trm:pulal-maruttal"], "notes": "Tantra-level reference.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirumantiram:tantra.2", "source": "src:tirumantiram", "location": {"ref": "tantra.2"}, "paraphrase": "The second tantra tells Śiva's great deeds and his five acts, and teaches that souls are of three classes — those with one mala, with two, and with three (vijñānākala, pralayākala, sakala).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["world-fate", "consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-classes-of-souls", "cpt:five-acts-of-siva"], "terms": ["trm:sakala", "trm:pralayakala", "trm:vijnanakala"], "notes": "Tantra-level reference; placement of the three classes in tantra 2 moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirumantiram:tantra.3", "source": "src:tirumantiram", "location": {"ref": "tantra.3"}, "paraphrase": "The third tantra teaches eightfold yoga — restraints, observances, postures, breath control, withdrawal, holding, meditation and absorption — and describes the eight powers (aṭṭamācitti) and other attainments that follow from it.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation", "body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "powers-experiences"], "practices": ["prc:tirumantiram-astanga-yoga"], "notes": "Tantra-level reference.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirumantiram:tantra.4", "source": "src:tirumantiram", "location": {"ref": "tantra.4"}, "paraphrase": "The fourth tantra teaches mantras and diagrams (cakkaram), especially the diagram of the five letters of the sacred hall (tiruvampalac cakkaram), and the worship of the Goddess (Śakti) as Śiva's power.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "ritual"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["sound-language", "practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:pancaksara"], "notes": "Tantra-level reference.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirumantiram:tantra.5", "source": "src:tirumantiram", "location": {"ref": "tantra.5"}, "paraphrase": "The fifth tantra distinguishes the Śaiva schools (pure, impure, 'path', and severe-pure Śaiva) and teaches the four paths — caryā, kriyā, yoga and jñāna — each containing the others in miniature, leading to the worlds, nearness, form and union with Śiva.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["action", "ritual", "meditation", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-padas", "cpt:four-kinds-of-mukti"], "paths": ["pth:saiva-siddhanta-four-padas"], "notes": "Tantra-level reference.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirumantiram:tantra.9", "source": "src:tirumantiram", "location": {"ref": "tantra.9"}, "paraphrase": "The ninth tantra sings the Dance (tirukkūttu) of Śiva in the hall of Tillai, which is also within the body and the heart, and the experience of Śiva beyond the tattvas.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "world-fate"], "concepts": ["cpt:dance-of-nataraja"], "notes": "Tantra-level reference.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
